  "body": "## Problem\nBot 4 correctly applied the exact Vinted `Galaxy S25` model filter, but after the current scan returned no genuinely new rows it processed two persisted `DISCOVERED` backlog entries with catalog identities `Samsung Galaxy Tab Active 3` and `Samsung Galaxy Tab S`.\n\nThe VINTED_MODEL guard considered those labels ambiguous because neither contains a compact model key such as `s24`/`s25`, so Playwright opened the live item pages even though the explicit `Galaxy Tab` family already proves they are not a Galaxy S25 phone.\n\n## Fix\n- treat the explicit Vinted model-family token `tab` as conclusive cross-family evidence when the configured model is not a Tab target\n- keep generic seller wording such as `Tablet i ładowarka` ambiguous so we do not over-classify arbitrary titles\n- preserve existing exact-model, variant and technical-code protections\n\n## Regression coverage\n- `Galaxy Tab Active 3` vs `Galaxy S25` => MISMATCH\n- `Galaxy Tab S` vs `Galaxy S25` => MISMATCH\n- existing `Galaxy Tab S9 FE+`, Fold/Flip, S24/S25 Ultra and generic-title behavior remains covered\n- integration coverage through `ListingTargetMatcher`",
